#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119616 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119805 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "fd3cb5b1-f16e-5a52-82e4-25bbbd1c4fe7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4789" :question/problem "Find $s,$ if $3\\mathbf{a_1}+s\\mathbf{a_2} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](images/c7/c715fd50dbcc9251cd7c01e033ba59be2af244d57ec02b707aa7cd8764e58d58.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $s$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+s{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $s=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119617 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119806 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "548ef945-392b-5e75-9b60-14f4e2de6261" :question/math-academy-id "e-4790" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{x},$ if $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](images/8f/8fef8bb1e88ca823b49d8c5544c5456c66b7a5beb0c9bd48f349a50bf3fa17b5.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $\\mathbf{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119618 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "13ebde04-8518-5837-9420-c9487debc562" :question/math-academy-id "e-4791" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n![](images/0b/0b7919416954fe536a93f681fb3c56cac8dddff67e389ef233fdb242390dfb91.svg)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then what is $x_1+x_2?$" :question/worked-solution "If $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1} &=-5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain $x_1=5,$ which we substitute into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ 4(5)+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 3(5)+(-15) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15,$ which means\n\n$$\n5 \\mathbf{c_1}-15 \\mathbf{c_2} = \\mathbf{d}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2=5-15=-10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119669 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "d9beff9d-db58-540f-811e-a07fb77d3d92" :question/math-academy-id "e-6191" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n![](images/16/1687c0a08fedfd90a26481007bb9bf56263edf67574fd690662064ef0341c86c.svg)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{a}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{a}_3 = \\mathbf b,$ then what is $x_1+x_2+x_3?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{b}$ is a linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{a_1}, \\,\\mathbf{a_2}$ and $\\mathbf{a_3}$ with coefficients $x_1,\\, x_2$ and $x_3,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n![](images/9b/9bf913744317fab321cf9f2e01da732853a52a4fd7948c65da596ae4706f6dce.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 = 2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_3=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+2(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=-3, x_2=-1, x_3=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3 \\mathbf{a_1}- \\mathbf{a_2} +2 \\mathbf{a_3}= \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2+x_3=-3-1+2=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119805 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ae96c9c-5077-5b4e-bce5-938adb6a5bc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238280} {:answer/id #uuid "33c2cd95-5c08-5d5a-9e16-58443a45fdf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238503} {:answer/id #uuid "3d876cfd-c9a8-56e1-ae3b-34704eccf96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238591} {:answer/id #uuid "88b9849d-4e76-5a49-87a7-7174e3308593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239243} {:answer/id #uuid "8d4e7316-49d2-54a2-8310-bd6fdca5c7cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ae96c9c-5077-5b4e-bce5-938adb6a5bc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238280} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d2aa0b0-6bd4-510a-8baa-0533d84db54e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b99af0d8-b75f-54bf-9697-c5d904e35653" :question/math-academy-id "q-105152" :question/problem "Find $h$, if $3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $h$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+h\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ h\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ h\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $h=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119806 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "078a9ec2-ec45-5cb3-9fa6-fafc704f3a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238137} {:answer/id #uuid "0fc0872c-5cbc-50aa-a104-55f19e6b295e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238190} {:answer/id #uuid "3859506a-2f62-51f2-9746-b6b6e6ad359c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238543} {:answer/id #uuid "7b700677-9bf6-5789-9d49-4fae8f9135eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239119} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a5b1bf-85fc-59df-966b-dfb82ea3d6cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b700677-9bf6-5789-9d49-4fae8f9135eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239119} :answer-field/id #uuid "e10a3090-0273-566f-800d-479ce03b72bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240725}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "308d5a63-8dfe-5681-a74a-191ce78c4eb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-105160" :question/problem "Find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ given that $3a-5x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-5x & =b \\\\ -5x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}(\\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+2=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf8efcb6-f1b1-576a-a750-35914835105a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371501} {:answer/id #uuid "f03805a7-390e-5218-9aba-0d3067bb4713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371502} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc31602-b9d2-56f8-a57a-90749cf42c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371503} {:answer/id #uuid "ea94efc8-3987-5798-8f16-29bc2348a033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371504} {:answer/id #uuid "c15415b1-26d3-51b7-9cfa-09a0452f811d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fc31602-b9d2-56f8-a57a-90749cf42c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371503} :answer-field/id #uuid "22d80b2a-30bb-5d27-bb13-817743c9301f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1eebc51b-6af1-57eb-9255-9e266158abc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-105171" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-5{x}_{2} \\\\ -8{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=9 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -8 & 2 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -8 & 2 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=7 \\\\ 0 &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=2$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240995 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43158102-a49d-59d4-a923-5df48591288f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238639} {:answer/id #uuid "7f08fc6f-64b7-5004-936e-7a6c7b50f76f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239160} {:answer/id #uuid "c032bb3d-2af4-5439-b0a3-83a63b9db908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239727} {:answer/id #uuid "c25ef7e8-5b9c-591c-b034-15f9595ed22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239760} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d1ebe2-d9a0-588f-835e-881ce34c1378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43158102-a49d-59d4-a923-5df48591288f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238639} :answer-field/id #uuid "83fca8c2-1efe-5ca1-813a-6af2b882ac08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e25147c5-4650-58c3-bac2-7139801cca6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-105172" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -5{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4{x}_{2} \\\\ -21{x}_{2} \\\\ -12{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 14{x}_{3} \\\\ 9{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-21{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-21{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3} &=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3} &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -21 & 14 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -21 & 14 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 18 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=18 \\\\ 0 &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=-1$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314969 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119806 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d4842ff-27f9-5992-9863-d07fd39b2d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312330} {:answer/id #uuid "36d9c331-1296-56e1-867e-1c1f15f8f9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312417} {:answer/id #uuid "4c387986-defc-56bc-8a0b-b8a9ac845695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312591} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa0ebec-880a-5969-86bd-143812e540c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312955} {:answer/id #uuid "a53d677f-0b4d-534d-a14a-e041a7519e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d4842ff-27f9-5992-9863-d07fd39b2d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312330} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea08bcfb-fe15-5af4-8217-ba4d412e8115" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314653}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a30a8dd5-ba00-5881-9097-ff69e821d30a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34052" :question/problem "Find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ given that $3a-5x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -22 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-5x & =b \\\\ -5x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}(\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -22 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3-1=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119805 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33982a47-2adf-5799-8859-c34bed20a404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315422} {:answer/id #uuid "5687a31f-ebd2-5317-b3f8-3e2eae8a8565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315615} {:answer/id #uuid "93d32481-f69e-5005-9fba-39aac45998ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315942} {:answer/id #uuid "e65cf7c4-b06f-5fb6-ae22-a85e9d62118e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316393} {:answer/id #uuid "fd275a29-c2ad-592a-9be5-c71e7051b5cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5687a31f-ebd2-5317-b3f8-3e2eae8a8565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315615} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b6e91e2-8f56-510a-b9e8-f88a07dd99b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ce5d7202-47f0-50c1-9bc6-a025b8d27432" :question/math-academy-id "q-34241" :question/problem "Find $j$, if ${a}_{1}-j{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $j$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}-j{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-j\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ j\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ j\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $j=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317259 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12b2fa0c-2460-5194-a41e-65210aaf675c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315229} {:answer/id #uuid "2d891e0d-7387-5fcc-8ea8-042f1f7dd10c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315384} {:answer/id #uuid "2f2e1fe7-1207-5eb3-84b2-aaed65147761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315386} {:answer/id #uuid "70266867-8c0a-5fdb-8194-68cd47f75152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315749} {:answer/id #uuid "92550deb-3f5e-5d93-8785-214a7b0242bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d891e0d-7387-5fcc-8ea8-042f1f7dd10c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315384} :answer-field/id #uuid "fda88ab2-6a42-5e3d-a747-d9d379dda047" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8179ffc2-2381-5ec9-a386-111d6e4cae85" :question/math-academy-id "q-34242" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,d=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0 &=4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe first equation is a false statement. Hence,the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8747e1ec-5bdc-5604-985b-58468728da61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117994} {:answer/id #uuid "bf310542-d18d-58a7-8e58-a22420156a7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117995} {:answer/id #uuid "cc90ae26-d46f-5f50-bd00-0e92bd416881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117996} {:answer/id #uuid "5599f481-dd85-552e-af10-eea6867254c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117997} {:answer/id #uuid "71e2eba5-06c7-50b6-88b0-7ea8c256dfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117998}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c343bbfd-7cc0-5884-946e-aa6090814a96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117993}] :question/id #uuid "6f395246-75c5-52ab-b275-6f768034cd27" :question/math-academy-id "q-34243" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, a_{3} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nIf $x_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2} + x_{3}a_{3} = b$, then what is $x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119806 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70f4e517-836c-5c50-977e-ad1416e94c03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393378} {:answer/id #uuid "ca13c47e-67cf-5d77-8541-fd0214e43fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393379} {:answer/id #uuid "3e6d5bf3-b9e8-5b63-9120-600dc92fcf16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393380} {:answer/id #uuid "00253e0b-d3bd-580f-a09c-d8e1132260ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393381} {:answer/id #uuid "dd936bbe-f994-551d-92c8-7ca23c711e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860